                <pb facs="0960" n="858" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg858"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">818.00/872: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at San José</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Chase</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San José</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-09-03T08:00:00-05:36"><hi rendition="#italic">September 3,
                                1919, 8 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received
                            September 5, 11.37 a.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>[Francisco] Aguilar Barquero in control of the country as Provisional President.
                    Everything apparently secure. I expect to see him again today and will telegraph
                    further developments.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Chase</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
